 # Custom Hardware Rendering
 ## Overview
-Custom Hardware Rendering is a direct volume rendering technique implemented via custom hardware rather than general-purpose processors [S2, unofficial]. It addresses the historical demand for real-time volume rendering systems when CPUs and GPUs lacked sufficient throughput [S1]. Unlike software-based approaches, these systems offload the rendering pipeline to fixed-function hardware, achieving interactive frame rates for regular data sets through highly parallel computation [S1]. It builds on [Direct volume ray casting](19-direct-volume-ray-casting.md) and [Hardware-Accelerated Volume Rendering](5616-hardware-accelerated-volume-rendering.md), and is distinct from [Hardware-based Geometry Unit Resampling](3139-hardware-based-geometry-unit-resampling.md) and [Hardware-based Direct Volume Ray Casting](5442-hardware-based-direct-volume-ray-casting.md).
+Custom Hardware Rendering is a direct volume rendering technique implemented via custom hardware rather than general-purpose processors [S2, unofficial]. It addresses the historical demand for real-time volume rendering systems when CPUs and GPUs lacked sufficient throughput [S1]. Unlike software-based approaches, these systems offload the rendering pipeline to fixed-function hardware, achieving interactive frame rates for regular data sets through highly parallel computation [S1].
 
