 ## Background
-Custom hardware rendering emerged in the late 1990s when CPUs and GPUs could not meet the real-time requirements for volume rendering [S1]. Key systems included Cube [KK99], Vizard [KS97], and VolumePro [PHK* 99]. Cube, based on a Shear-Warp hybrid algorithm, was the predecessor to VolumePro [S1]. VolumePro evolved to include separate sample and voxel processing pipelines, improving scalability but still lacking perspective support in its earlier generations [S1]. These systems were developed for rendering regular data sets [S1].
